<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ying Bu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 196 BCE</span> · Also known as Qing Bu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ying Bu was a Chinese general who rebelled against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin dynasty</a> and served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a>, who made him King of Jiujiang in 206 BCE. He went over to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a> during the Chu–Han contention and was made King of Huainan. Fearing the purge of other kings, he rebelled against the Han in 196 BCE and was killed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ying-bu.jpg" alt="Ying Bu" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 鍾 惺, 1574-1624 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WUL-he21_01467_%E6%96%B0%E9%90%AB%E7%B9%AA%E5%83%8F%E6%9D%B1%E8%A5%BF%E6%BC%A2%E5%85%A8%E5%82%B3_01_(%E8%8B%B1%E5%B8%83).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
